# No automatic browser or build checks

After an edit, stop. The user checks the running app themselves.

- Do not open localhost or use browser tools (`browser_navigate`, snapshots, screenshots, CDP `Runtime.evaluate`, clicks) unless the user explicitly asks to look at the page.
- Do not search or read `.next` to confirm an edit reached the dev server.
- Do not run `pnpm build`, `next build`, or a production build after an edit. Run one only when the user asks, or when the task is a build failure, a deploy check, or a change that only shows up at build time.

```text
// After editing components/header.tsx
// Stop. Do not open http://localhost:3000.
// Do not grep .next for the new prop.
// Do not run pnpm build.
```
